findings.body:
The emitter in `XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs` was changed in three ways: the null guard, `p.Name == propertyName` (was `metadata.Name`), `operation.Summary = remarks`, and the RequestBody reorder. Only the null guard was propagated to the snapshots. The eight existing `*.generated.verified.cs` snapshots still contain `p.Name == metadata.Name` and `operation.Description = remarks`. The new `SupportsRouteParametersFromControllers` snapshot also has the old text, so its content no longer matches what the generator emits.

The snapshot tests compare generator output with the verified file, so they will fail on every run. The reviewer cannot tell which side is intended.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="444-452"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Either regenerate every affected snapshot after the emitter is finalized, or revert the unrelated emitter edits. Do not leave the two out of sync.

The `<remarks>` tag used to populate `operation.Description`. This PR changes it to `operation.Summary`, so `<remarks>` now replaces the `<summary>` text. The description says nothing about this, and it changes the output of any controller or minimal API that uses `<remarks>`.

The `Summary`-then-`Remarks` order means a `<remarks>` block wins over `<summary>`. That is almost certainly not intended: `<remarks>` is long-form description text and belongs in `Description`, as it did before.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="380-383"}

::suggestion{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="380-383"}
if (methodComment.Remarks is { } remarks)
{
    operation.Description = remarks;
}

The original mapping (`Remarks` to `Description`) should stay. If the Summary change is intended, it belongs in a separate PR with its own description and tests.

The RequestBody description assignment was moved from before the example block to after it. Inside the example block there is an early `continue` when `operation.RequestBody.Content?.Values` is null. That `continue` now skips the trailing `operation.RequestBody.Description = description;`, so the description is silently dropped whenever the example is present and the content is null.

Before this PR the description was always set first, so this path did not lose it. The move is unrelated to the null-metadata fix and it introduces a regression.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="464-481"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The move is not needed for the fix. Put the description assignment back before the example block.

::suggestion{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="464-466"}
if (operation.RequestBody is not null)
{
    operation.RequestBody.Description = description;
    if (propertyComment.Examples?.FirstOrDefault() is { } jsonString)

The first three lines of `XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs` were deleted: the Microsoft .NET Foundation license header. The base revision has it, and the sibling file `XmlCommentGenerator.cs` still has it. The description does not mention the removal, so it is most likely accidental.

Repository tooling and reviewers expect this header on every source file. It can also trip license or header checks in CI.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="1-3"}

The parameter lookup now matches `p.Name == propertyName` instead of `p.Name == metadata.Name`. For property metadata these are usually equal, but that is not guaranteed. The PR description does not mention this change, so it is unclear why it was made.

If it is intended, it is a behavior change that should be explained and tested. If not, it is scope creep that adds risk without a corresponding fix. Either way, the snapshots still use `metadata.Name`.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="452-452"}

The new `SupportsRouteParametersFromControllers` test checks `path.Parameters[0].Description`, which is good. It does not confirm that the controller route parameter arrives with a null `ModelMetadata`, the condition that caused the original NullReferenceException. If the framework later populates metadata for this route, the test would still pass and stop guarding the regression.

I could not run the test, so I cannot say whether it fails on the base revision. Confirming that it fails before the fix would make it a real regression test.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/test/Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi.SourceGenerators.Tests/OperationTests.Controllers.cs" lines="100-143"}

The core change is well scoped. The guard is added at the point where `ModelMetadata` is read, and it reuses the existing pattern-matching condition, so the branch is skipped cleanly when metadata is null.

::diff{file="src/OpenApi/gen/XmlCommentGenerator.Emitter.cs" lines="444-447"}

The same guard is applied consistently to the eight other generated snapshots, which is the right shape for this fix.
